From: Marek Andrzejewski <marek1and@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Close the audio output when the stream ends

At the end of the last track core sets STOPPED, but playbin stays in
PLAYING, so pulsesink keeps an uncorked stream with no data open on the
audio server. pipewire-pulse 1.6 advances the read index of such a stream
on every underrun cycle; its signed 32-bit fill level wraps after 2^31
bytes (93 min at 48 kHz stereo F32LE) and it then plays the last 4 MB of
its ring buffer again: the last ~11 s of the track, every ~93 min.

Stop playback at end of stream, the same as an explicit stop.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/mopidy/core/_actor.py | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mopidy/core/_actor.py b/src/mopidy/core/_actor.py
index d484d86..4f36a43 100644
--- a/src/mopidy/core/_actor.py
+++ b/src/mopidy/core/_actor.py
@@ -116,6 +116,10 @@ class Core(
     @override
     def reached_end_of_stream(self) -> None:
         self.playback._on_end_of_stream()
+        # Close the output: a sink left playing without data keeps an
+        # uncorked stream open on the audio server.
+        if self.audio:
+            self.audio.stop_playback()
 
     @override
     def stream_changed(self, uri: Uri) -> None:
